# =============================================================================
#  deploy.conf  ·  copy to <your-repo>/_deploy/deploy.conf and fill it in
# =============================================================================
#  deploy.sh sources this file, so it is shell: NO spaces around `=`, and quotes
#  where quotes are needed.
#
#  Until this file exists, the door refuses to open and says what is missing.
#  That is the only honest posture: better a closed door than one that opens by
#  itself onto a site nobody has checked.
#
#  TREAT THIS FILE AS CODE. The door executes the command you put in UPLOAD.
#  The system deliberately does not know how to upload anything, which is why it
#  cannot upload anywhere you did not name.
# =============================================================================

# The root URL. The served-equals-measured check builds its URLs from this.
SITE=https://your-domain.tld

# A RETIRED DOMAIN whose tree is only a robots.txt and an .htaccess that sends
# everything with 301 to another site: declare it, and the receipt comes from
# gates/redirects-gate.pl --candidate instead of qa-master.pl. The door then says
# NOT APPLICABLE out loud for the steps that measure pages, and after the upload
# asks the domain for every mapped path and the WordPress ones (step 4-ter).
# A page in such a tree makes the receipt invalid. Default: pages.
# TREE=redirects

# The command that uploads THE WHOLE TREE. Either:
#   · a path relative to the repo   -> run with bash
#   · a complete command
#
# WARNING: what it cannot be is a command that uploads only part of the tree.
# If it uploads only the CSS, the served-equals-measured step will compare the N
# files in the receipt against what is served and report the rest as missing.
# That is correct behaviour, not a false red — and it is the single most common
# reason a first deploy comes out red. Either upload everything, or accept that
# the check is telling you the truth about a partial upload.
UPLOAD=_deploy/upload.sh

# ── Browser step: the things only a browser can see ──────────────────────────
# Runs TWICE (2026-11-01, traps §89):
# - BEFORE the upload (step 1-quater), on the tree about to go up: structure,
#   screen density, mobile at 360/390/1366/1440 and the mobile menu at 390. A
#   FAIL STOPS the upload. Going up anyway takes an --aun-asi that names each red
#   gate; a motive saying "the browser answers it" is refused.
# - AFTER the upload (step 6), on what is served, with the forms gate. It does
#   not block; it records its verdict in the history file.
#
# IMPORTANT: run this from a Linux host with a real Chrome. On Windows, headless
# Chrome clamps the window width to about 500px, so a measurement "at 390"
# actually describes a page laid out at 504 and the screenshot is a crop. Ask
# any probe for its innerWidth and refuse the number if it does not match.

# Which pages get measured for layout and density. Default: the home page only.
# With this line set, a page the browser could not measure before the upload
# also stops it, unless the --aun-asi says why.
BROWSER_URLS="/ /contact/"

# Where this site takes bookings, besides the platforms the gates already know
# (space-separated host names; see blueprint/20-external-booking.md). A button
# to one of them counts as converting. It says WHERE booking happens; the hero
# button still has to go there.
# BOOKING_HOSTS="mybookingplatform.example"

# A shop: the hero may lead to the catalogue instead of converting on the page.
# ECOMMERCE=1

# How many browser measurements run at once on the measuring host (default 3).
# NAV_PARALELO=3

# The brand gate (marca-gate.js) only WARNS until you set this. Set it once the
# site's brand file, _diseno/MARCA.md, is done (palette under «## Colores», type
# under «## Tipos») and its icons are in place: from then on a missing icon or a
# colour outside the palette stops the upload like any other browser gate.
# MARCA_GATE=para

# Third-party widgets whose colours are not the brand's (a chat bubble, a
# consent tool you cannot style): comma-separated CSS selectors, left out of
# the palette count. Only letters, digits, # . _ and -.
# MARCA_IGNORAR="#chat-widget, .third-party-badge"

# The other browser gates that only WARN until the site asks them to stop the upload:
# the buttons (botones-gate.js, once its buttons are unified), the cookie notice
# (banner-probe.js) and what the visitor sees (visible-gate.js: content still
# invisible after scrolling, a Tab stop hidden whole under a sticky header or a
# fixed bar; the usual fix is html{scroll-padding-top:<header height>}), and the
# marks of a page made in series (huellas-gate.js: a kicker over every section
# heading, gradient text, a one-sided border on a rounded box, a coloured glow,
# transition: all, tight leading, a heading ending on one word, a phone field that
# rejects a valid number).
# BOTONES_GATE=para
# BANNER_GATE=para
# VISIBLE_GATE=para
# HUELLAS_GATE=para

# Which pages have a form. On these, the form step is REQUIRED: a page here that
# ends up without a working form is a FAIL, not a "does not apply". Without this
# line the form step IS NOT MEASURED, and that gets recorded — an unmeasured
# form is not a correct one.
FORM_URLS="/contact/"

# A site with NO GA4 and NO Google Ads, by decision: the conversion lands
# somewhere else (a booking calendar, an inbox). MED-13 (a conversion that
# reached GA4 or Ads) is then NOT APPLICABLE at the door, with this reason, and
# gates/d057.pl checks that the tree really carries no tag: if a page loads
# gtag, Tag Manager or an AW- id, the upload stops instead. Without this line
# MED-13 stays NOT VERIFIED. The door reads NO_GA4_OR_ADS or SIN_GA4_NI_ADS.
# NO_GA4_OR_ADS="bookings land in the calendar; no analytics or ads, decided on 2026-10-19"

# A site WITH GA4 and NO Google Ads campaign running. MED-13 asks for a
# conversion in the Ads interface, which such a site never has: with this line
# qa-master measures MED-13 in GA4 instead (the lead event is a key event and it
# has been seen arriving), and prints the DATO to sign it with in measured.conf.
# The tree is checked: a page carrying AW-, googleadservices.com or
# googleads.g.doubleclick.net makes MED-13 a FAIL. Remove the line the day the
# campaigns start: the signature stops counting on its own, and MED-13 asks for
# the conversion in Ads again. qa-master reads NO_ADS or SIN_ADS.
# NO_ADS="no campaigns until the launch planned for December"

# The PUBLISHED page's DOM, for gates/d057.pl. A FAIL that comes from the browser
# snapshot (EST-05/06/07, REN-11: the candidate was measured with --dom) can only
# be compared with production through production's own snapshot: without it,
# d057 says NOT MEASURED for those, never "old" and never "new". Capture it on
# the measuring host, on the live page that --dom described, at the SAME width
# and height as the candidate's, less than 12 hours before the upload:
#   perl gates/qa-master.pl --snippet > qa.js
#   node gates/run-gate.js https://your-domain.tld/ 390 844 qa.js | tail -n +2 > _deploy/dom-production.json
# A path relative to the repo. The door reads D057_PRODUCTION_DOM or D057_DOM_PRODUCCION.
# D057_PRODUCTION_DOM=_deploy/dom-production.json

# A measurement only the served site can answer, that this door cannot bring by
# itself: for example, the URLs with impressions in Search Console that were left
# without a 301 (before the upload production still answers 200 to all of them, so
# a URL the candidate drops without its 301 looks the same as one that carries it).
# The door runs it from the repo after G11 and the browser (step 6-ter), and it
# only WARNS: what was uploaded is uploaded. Exit 0 is PASS, 1 is a WARNING with
# the lines that say FAIL or WARN, anything else (or 10 minutes) NOT MEASURED. It
# goes into the closing line and the history. The door reads AFTER_UPLOAD or TRAS_SUBIR.
# Paths with forward slashes, also on Windows (C:/Users/...): the command goes
# through `bash -c`, which eats backslashes, and the door says so when it happens.
# AFTER_UPLOAD="node /path/to/your-tools/urls-dropped.mjs --site your-domain.tld"

# Skip the browser step entirely, with a reason. It still gets recorded: a
# declared hole is still a hole. Useful when the site is not reachable from the
# measuring host.
# NO_BROWSER=1

# Where to measure from: an ssh alias for a Linux host with Chrome and puppeteer.
# The measuring host usually belongs to the MACHINE, not to one site, so the
# normal place for it is gates/config/nav-host.local.conf (one line,
# NAV_HOST=your-ssh-alias; *.conf is gitignored). Set it here only if this site
# needs a different host. If neither is set, the browser step says
# "NO MEDIDO: NAV_HOST sin configurar" and measures nothing: until 21-sep-2026
# it silently tried a placeholder host instead, and 77 deploys went unmeasured.
# The door reads BROWSER_HOST or NAV_HOST (and BROWSER_URLS / URLS_NAVEGADOR,
# FORM_URLS / URLS_FORMULARIO, NO_BROWSER / SIN_NAVEGADOR).
# BROWSER_HOST=your-measuring-host
